{"cluster_id": "C-1122", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B019-041", "B019-044", "B019-050", "B019-054", "B019-056"], "canonical_claim": "The COW overlay is scoped to `RefTableState::committed`; `precommits` remains `std::set`, only `committed` changes, the base remains `std::map` in this cut, the codec remains based on `std::vector<RefCommittedRow>`, and an optional future `absl::btree_map` follow-up is allowed. It uses a sorted `std::map` because ordered merge iteration is required; a persistent immutable ordered tree is deferred because no drop-in implementation exists in the tree.; The persistent ordered-tree approach, an `absl::btree_map` base, and changes to `precommits` are out of scope for the COW-map cut; commit-path tracing and microbenchmark evidence are separate follow-up work.; A persistent immutable ordered tree is deferred, `absl::btree_map` is optional follow-up work, and `precommits` remains unchanged.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-cas-reftable-cow-map.md#L1249-L1257", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-cas-reftable-cow-map.md#L13-L31", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-17-cas-reftable-cow-map-design.md#L17-L28", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-17-cas-reftable-cow-map-design.md#L38-L42", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-17-cas-reftable-cow-map-design.md#L54-L58"]}
