{"cluster_id": "C-1128", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B023-043", "B023-112"], "canonical_claim": "The rev.7 lifecycle plan rolls back the landed Dormant/UNMOUNT reuse lifecycle after switching tests to `DROP SYNC \u2192 FORGET \u2192 verify \u2192 rm -rf`; the abort hardening, coherent `poolAccess()` snapshot, atomic `startup()`, and `ca-fsck` rename are retained.; The landed Dormant/UNMOUNT lifecycle is unsound because its benign-absent behavior can silently skip reclaim and make ATTACH load an empty table when data may still exist.", "issue_ids": ["C1", "C10", "C2", "C3", "rev.7"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-22-cas-disk-lifecycle-rev7.md#L375-L411", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-disk-lifecycle-problem-and-constraints.md#designs-tried-and-why-each-is-unsound"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1129", "topic": "design-history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B024-003", "B024-070"], "canonical_claim": "Stage 1 is limited to CAS-internal changes plus minimal pool server wiring, with no behavioral seam in `MergeTree` or generic-Disks code, and validates parallel blob upload within a part; cross-part `commitPart` concurrency/dispatch is deferred to stage 2 as the larger cross-part upload-concurrency opportunity.", "issue_ids": ["S41"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-23-cas-wide-insert-baseline.md#verdict-for-stage-1-gate", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-22-cas-writepath-stage1-internal-design.md#design"]}
